    "title": "Flags order to half-staff in Kentucky after Charlie Kirk's death - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dustin Massengill ,\n1 days ago\nFRANKFORT, Ky. ( FOX 56 ) — Gov. Andy Beshear has ordered all state flags to be lowered to half-staff until sunset on Sept. 14, after conservative influencer Charlie Kirk died on Wednesday.\nKirk, 31, died after being shot while speaking at Utah Valley University in Orem.\nLATEST KENTUCKY NEWS: Bullitt County tattoo studio severs ties with artist for ‘celebrating’ death of conservative influencer Motive unknown in Perry County drive-by shooting Sen. McConnell secures funding to fight opioid addiction in Kentucky “I strongly condemn the senseless attack on Charlie Kirk today. Political violence has no place in the United States of America. It further tears our country apart and sets us back versus moving us forward. Violence is always wrong. Period,” Beshear said on X.\nThe governor also directed that flags be lowered to half-staff on Thursday, Sept. 11, in commemoration of Patriot Day and in honor of those lost in the 9/11 attacks.\nGov. Beshear encourages individuals, businesses, and organizations throughout the commonwealth to join in this tribute.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 56 News.\n2",
